 keepalive                       v2.0.0

 KEYS
 [↑↓] choose how long
 [⏎]  start
 [?]  this help
 [q]  quit
 [a]  simulate activity
 [d]  keep the display on
 [b]  stop at a battery level
 [k]  tap Shift with activity

 Simulate activity makes small pointer
 arcs (up to 130 px) once you are idle,
 so Teams and Slack show you as Active.
 It pauses while you use the computer
 or the screen is locked; "keepalive
 doctor" checks that it works.
 Logs: off; start with --log to write
 /home/u/.cache/keepalive/keepalive.log

 [esc] close  [ctrl+c] quit
